    family: "Parents St. Louis Martin (watchmaker) and St. Zélie Guérin (lacemaker), canonized together on 18 October 2015 — the first married couple canonized as a couple. Nine children; four died in infancy. Thérèse was the youngest of the five surviving daughters, and all five became nuns: Marie (Sr. Marie of the Sacred Heart), Pauline (Mother Agnes of Jesus, later prioress), Léonie (Sr. Françoise-Thérèse, a Visitandine, whose cause is open), Céline (Sr. Geneviève of the Holy Face), and Thérèse. Zélie died of breast cancer when Thérèse was four.",
