    relics: "His body was carried from Hippo to Sardinia to escape the Vandals, and then bought from the Saracens by King Liutprand of the Lombards around 720 and brought to Pavia. It lies in the Ark of St Augustine, a 14th-century marble shrine, in San Pietro in Ciel d'Oro, Pavia — the church Dante mentions in the Paradiso. Relics were returned to Annaba, Algeria, in 1842.",
