    forYou: "Benedict's Rule is arguably the single most 'implementable' spiritual routine in Church history precisely because it's a schedule, not a philosophy. You don't need eight hours of chant, but the underlying structure — fixed prayer times you don't skip regardless of mood, a real block of unhurried reading (not skimming), a defined work period, and a protected quiet transition into sleep — maps directly onto an ordinary week. The core principle worth stealing outright: let nothing be preferred to whatever your fixed prayer time is — treat it as non-negotiable scheduling, the way Benedict treated the Office.",
