    forYou: "As with Padre Pio, the extremity here (near-starvation, near-total sleep deprivation) is not the takeaway — even his own contemporaries thought he overdid it. The transferable practice is smaller and more concrete: he kept a short, plain daily instruction going even when totally overwhelmed by the bigger demand (the confessional) — he didn't let the large obligation crowd out the small, regular one. If you have one small daily spiritual practice and a big demanding week, his example argues for keeping the small one rather than dropping it 'until things calm down.'",
