    controversies: "Her homes for the dying, especially Nirmal Hriday, drew sustained criticism over the decades (notably from journalist and physician critics) regarding limited medical care, pain management, and hygiene standards relative to available resources; defenders responded that the homes' explicit purpose was dignified accompaniment in death rather than curative medicine, a distinction that remains genuinely contested rather than fully resolved.",
