    context: "Geneva itself was the stronghold of Calvinism under Calvin's own former authority, and the Chablais region on Savoy's border had been forcibly Calvinist for decades; Francis's mission there through patient preaching and printed argument, rather than coercion, became a celebrated model of peaceable Counter-Reformation evangelization.",
