    stateOfLife: "Bishop, founder",
    context: "Catholic moral theology in his lifetime was pulled between rigorism (which risked driving penitents to despair or away from the sacraments) and laxism (which risked excusing real sin); Alphonsus's systematic moderate path, equiprobabilism, became the dominant approach for the following century and more.",
