    forYou: "Joseph's case argues against a common assumption: that a serious daily spiritual practice needs to look impressive or be recognized by anyone. He spent years doing kitchen work nobody thought was spiritually significant, with no outward sign of anything unusual, before anything visible happened — and he accepted decades more of quiet, unrecognized restriction afterward without resentment. If your own daily practice feels small, hidden, or unnoticed by anyone else, that's not evidence it isn't real; by Joseph's example it might be exactly the ordinary ground holiness grows from.",
